<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">Leaders only</p>
    <h1>Backups</h1>
    <p class="lede measure">
      This board runs on Cloudflare's managed database and file storage, so
      there's no single file on a disk to zip up. What you get instead: a
      database snapshot you can download any time below, plus a copy that's
      already made automatically without anyone clicking anything.
    </p>

    <div class="card <%= backupStale ? 'card--warn' : '' %>">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted">Your last download</p>
      <p>
        <% if (lastBackupAt) { %>
          <span class="badge <%= backupStale ? 'badge--warn' : 'badge--ok' %>"><%= dates.relative(lastBackupAt) %></span>
        <% } else { %>
          <span class="badge badge--warn">Never downloaded</span>
        <% } %>
      </p>
      <p class="form-actions">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/admin/backup/download.sql">Download database snapshot (.sql)</a>
      </p>
      <p class="hint hint--block">
        A plain-text SQL file with every member, post, announcement, meeting,
        draft record and comment as <span class="mono">INSERT</span>
        statements — open it in any text editor, or load it into a fresh
        database with the <span class="mono">sqlite3</span> command line. It
        does <strong>not</strong> include the draft, event or chat files
        themselves; see below for those. Downloading refreshes the "last
        backed up" badge on the <a href="/admin">admin dashboard</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted">Automatic monthly snapshot</p>
      <p>
        <% if (lastSnapshotAt) { %>
          A copy is also written automatically to Cloudflare storage on the
          1st of every month, whether or not anyone downloads one by hand.
          Most recent: <span class="badge badge--ok"><%= dates.relative(lastSnapshotAt) %></span>
          (<%= lastSnapshotMonth %>).
        <% } else { %>
          <span class="badge badge--warn">Not run yet</span> — this happens on
          its own on the 1st of the month; there's nothing to click for it.
        <% } %>
      </p>
      <p class="hint hint--block">
        This is a belt-and-braces copy sitting alongside your own downloads,
        not a replacement for them — it protects against nobody remembering
        to click Download for months at a stretch, not against needing a
        backup at all.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted">The files themselves</p>
      <p class="measure">
        Uploaded drafts, off-site event attachments and chat attachments live
        in Cloudflare's file storage (R2), organized the same way they always
        were on disk:
      </p>
      <ul class="mono small">
        <% r2Prefixes.forEach(function (prefix) { %>
          <li><%= prefix %>…</li>
        <% }) %>
      </ul>
      <p class="measure">
        <span class="mono">backups/</span> is the automatic snapshots above,
        each month's folder holding one file per database table plus a
        <span class="mono">manifest.json</span> listing them.
      </p>
      <p class="measure">
        Copying any of those in bulk needs a terminal, not a browser button —
        a one-time setup for whoever holds the group's Cloudflare account, not
        a monthly chore:
      </p>
      <pre class="mono small" style="overflow-x: auto;">wrangler r2 object get afwc-board-files/&lt;key&gt; --file ./out --remote

# or the whole bucket, with rclone configured for an R2 access key:
rclone copy r2:afwc-board-files ./local-backup</pre>
      <p class="hint hint--block">
        Account ID and R2 API token setup for those commands is in the
        repository's README, not here — this page is the leader-facing half
        of the backup story; the README is the developer-facing half.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p><a class="btn btn--sm" href="/admin">Back to the dashboard</a></p>
  </div>
</section>
